# Cursor Rules — Skills Monorepo

You are working in a curated skill library. `AGENTS.md` is authoritative; this file is the short version.

## Read first

- `AGENTS.md` for invariants and protocol
- `registry/domains.json` to choose a domain
- `docs/SKILLS.md` for the full catalog

## Rules

1. Ground every change in real files. Read the target and its `SOURCE.json` before editing.
2. Skills with `"origin": "upstream"` are vendored verbatim. Never edit them.
3. New skills need `SKILL.md` and `SOURCE.json`. A description must say when to activate the skill.
4. New resources go in `resources/<category>.json` with `id`, `name`, `url`, `type`, `pricing`, `license`, `description`, `why`, and `tags`. HTTPS only.
5. Do not hand-edit `registry/*.json`, `docs/SKILLS.md`, `docs/RESOURCES.md`, or `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. They are generated.

## After changes

```bash
python3 scripts/build-registry.py
npm run validate
npm run docs
```

If validation fails, fix the cause. Do not relax the check to make it pass.

## Voice

Write plainly. No filler, no fabricated counts, no em dash chains.
